# Interpreter-throw closure item 6, the dynamically selected callable: a callee declaring a name does not fit the
# nameless contract `fn: (int: x) int` -- the admission by signature of section 7 refuses it at the actual, located
# ("incompatible entry signature"); the caller's `catch: Oops` is never reached by a dynamic callee today.
fn: boom (int: x) int
    throws: Oops
    throw: Oops(x)
    return: 81

fn: apply (op(fn: (int: x) int) int(value)) int
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: op(value)
    ---
    catch: Oops (int: v)
        got: 5 + v
return: got

int: r apply(boom 2)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
